==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Ackey]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Camelle]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*10 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[Ackey]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Ackey]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use units that are able to chip down Camelle by either tanking or rushing. By using as little meatshields as possible, the Ackeys will miss your attackers and do nothing.

[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used to rush the Camelle. Supercar can also be used to instantly kill an Ackey. [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] can  allow your rushers to survive for longer. [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]] can stall the Camelle easily and deal a decent amount of damage to it.

==Trivia==
*Boiling Blood's Japanese name, Chinoike Futtō (血の池沸騰, "Boiling Blood Pond"), may be a reference to [https://youtu.be/zaIYxcBuatA Chinoike Jigoku] (血の池地獄, "Blood Pond Hell"), one of the seven hot springs known as the [[wikipedia:Hells of Beppu|Hells of Beppu]].
**It could also be a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Divine Comedy|Divine Comedy]]'', in which the Seventh Circle of Hell contains a river of boiling blood, named after [[wikipedia:Phlegethon|Phlegethon]] from Greek mythology.

